Z||000000||85seNUT||12-21-2001||11:34 PM||||i go to college and i havent driven my car in more than 2 weeks and it has just been stting in the rain and cold.  i fired it up after these two weeks and it seemed to be fine.  but when i tried to drive it i had the slowest acceleration ever invented and once i reaced 3,000 or so rpms it doens get any power and wont go any farther.  I have never had any thing remotly related to this problem.  i have an 85 se with the 3.4 conversion and a 4 spd manual.  please help me.  i have checked the intake(not clogged), i have let it run and warm up for ever(didnt work) i looked at the distributor and cleaned it out(didnt work), checked the plugs(all seemed fine) checked the spark plugs, well at  least the front 3,(looked fine)  what could be the problem?  is it clocked injectors?  do they get like that if your car sits?  i dont get it.  please help.  thank you||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-21-2001||11:47 PM||||Sitting for a few weeks won't foul up your injectors (unless they were already starting to clog up).  I have owned/tinkered with Fieros that have sat unstarted for more than 13 years......all i needed to do was install a new fuel pump, but then they fired right up and had no issues.<P>It sounds like there is a plug somewhere.....my guess would be the catalytic convertor, but it is only a guess.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-22-2001||12:05 PM||||I agree with Mrfiero.....sounds like a clogged convertor to me too...good luck and Merry Christmas.<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT GT 87||12-22-2001||05:53 PM||||My '87 lost about 30% power in one day . It was the cat !!!!!!!!!!!!  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dumba$$||12-22-2001||10:58 PM||||convertor, fuel filter, fuel pump,<BR>are all good possibilities but , id check into the coil  it may be getting week<BR>that was my problem <BR>if you have or can get acess to a coil, plug it in (you probibly wouldnt need bolt it down just to go arround the block) and give it hell arround the block and see if it works<BR>Good luck<P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>ever notice that people that own a fiero, either have, or have had other fieros?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hairy_Fiero||12-23-2001||12:57 AM||||Sure sounds like the cat. convertor. Could be a number of things, but the cat. or the coil are the first that come to mind.||||reg||1
